Yes, it is possible to make an HTML element unmodifiable from JavaScript. This can be achieved by using the `setDocumentFragment()` method, which removes the element from the document and makes it unmodifiable. Here's an example of how you can do this:

```javascript
// Assuming you have an element with the id "myElement"
var myElement = document.getElementById("myElement");

// Make the element unmodifiable
myElement.setDocumentFragment();
```

This will remove the element from the document and make it unmodifiable. However, it's important to note that this approach is not recommended for production code, as it can lead to issues with the DOM and other JavaScript code that relies on the element's state.
